    intermediate: "The 'Pige' Bluff: If you see an opponent has only 3 cards left, they are close to going out. If a card is discarded that *might* help them, even if you don't need it, 'Pige' it to take it away. You are paying a 2-card penalty to stop them from winning. This is a defensive trade-off that is essential in the late-game rounds.",
